; Original Blitz3D side of the dungeon benchmark: the timer has milliseconds only, and there are no draw counters (0).

Function BenchMicros()
	Return MilliSecs() * 1000
End Function

Function BenchDraws()
	Return 0
End Function

Function BenchPipelines()
	Return 0
End Function

Function BenchTextures()
	Return 0
End Function

Function BenchBuffers()
	Return 0
End Function

; The original has no SpriteDepthFade, so the flames and smoke stay as they are.
Function BenchDepthFade(sprite, distance#)
End Function

; The original crashes with more sprites than that: they share one vertex buffer of 4 vertices each, which grows 256 sprites at a
; time, and Direct3D 7 refuses the step from 16128 sprites (64512 vertices) to 16384 (65536 vertices). The flame and smoke templates
; are sprites too, so 16128 - 2 = 16126 are left for the particles.
Function BenchMaxSprites()
	Return 16126
End Function

; Shows the frame without waiting for the display (the original has no Flip 2).
Function BenchFlip()
	Flip 0
End Function
